<title>USA: Excelsior-Henderson makes market debut.</title>
<headline>Excelsior-Henderson makes market debut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Excelsior-Henderson Motorcycle Manufacturing Co, which made its market debut on Thursday at an initial offering price of $7.50 per share, reached a Friday high of $8 a share before dipping to 7-17/32 less than an hour before today's close.</p>
<p>The four million share deal priced within the expected range of $7 - $8 per share, said underwriter John G Kinnard.</p>
<p>The company said in its filing that it set a two-for-three split on its outstanding common and preferred stock in connection with the IPO.</p>
<p>Excelsior plans to manufacture, market and sell American heavyweight cruiser and touring motorcycles.</p>
</text>
